@startuml update-push
title US-02: Update Push - Live Position Filtered by Scope Before Push

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

participant "Position\nConsumer" as Consumer
database "Redis\nentity:live:{id}" as Redis
participant "Express API\n(ws library)" as API
participant "Angular\nDashboard" as Dashboard
actor Operator

Consumer -> Redis : HSET entity:live:{entity_id}\n{ lat, lon, altitude, timestamp_ms, entity_type }
Consumer -> API : publish update via Redis pub/sub

note over API
  Redis pub/sub fans updates out
  across multiple API instances
  without duplicating Kafka consumption.
end note

loop for each active WebSocket connection
  note over API
    Each connection has a saved scope:
    { geo_region.bounds, entity_types, alert_types }
    Both position updates and alerts are filtered
    before being pushed to each client.
  end note

  alt entity position within scope geo bounds\nAND entity_type in scope.entity_types
    API -> Dashboard : push { entity_id, lat, lon,\n  altitude, entity_type, timestamp_ms }
    Dashboard -> Dashboard : update entity position on map
    Dashboard --> Operator : entity moves to new position
  else entity outside scope bounds or wrong type
    note over API
      Update is silently dropped for this connection.
      The operator's scope determines which entities
      appear on their map, not just which alerts they receive.
    end note
  end
end

note over Dashboard, Operator
  No HTTP request made.
  No page refresh required.
  Latency = network RTT only.
end note

@enduml
